(P116 - Pen up to the GP2 lift-home switch, then home X/Y and park off the bed.)
(Manual operator command for the converter's end-of-print clear -> full retract -> G53 park.)
(Intended for an ioSender button named PEN UP + PARK, confirmation enabled, issuing G65 P116.)
(It never runs a blind absolute move: step 3 is what makes the park frame known. An unhomed)
(controller has no machine frame and no soft-limit envelope, so a G53 park pressed from it)
(travels the whole commanded distance from wherever the gantry actually is.)
(It requires the installed Aux0/GP28 path - M65 asserts the arm, M64 releases it - the)
(toolhead M5 clearance, the disarmed-Aux0 full-retract behaviour, and P111 for the home.)

(Self-contained modal and frame setup, matching the converter program preamble.)
G21
G90
G94
G17
G54

(1. Normal pen-up, then prove the pen left the paper before anything moves.)
(Q0 accepts an already-clear level or waits for clear-ready; a stuck or faulted toolhead)
(raises error 39 and stops here, so no motion is attempted from contact.)
M5
G65 P115 Q0
(A controller without the installed P115.macro substitutes the converter's pen-up dwell:)
(G4 P0.8. That only bounds the clearance; it does not prove it.)

(2. Request the full retract to the GP2 lift-home switch through the Aux0/GP28 arm.)
(Release the arm and wait out the toolhead's 3.0 s MAG_REARM_WINDOW_MS before asserting)
(it again. That gap matters when the pen is already parked at GP2: with its readiness)
(prerequisites met, one assertion is a magnetic READY_ACK, and a second assertion inside)
(the rearm window would move the magnetic state into SCAN_ACTIVE instead of retracting.)
M64 P0
G4 P3.5
M65 P0
(3.0 s is the toolhead's own full-retract bound (BOOT_LIFT_TIME_MS). It reports)
(GP2 lift-home not reached during retract instead of retracting without a limit.)
G4 P3.0
M64 P0

(3. Physical X/Y home through the reviewed P111 macro, with the pen already retracted to)
(GP2. The homed position is the only reference that makes the park target meaningful, and)
(homing is what makes the controller build its soft-limit envelope for X and Y.)
G65 P111

(4. Park off the bed at the homed rest position in machine coordinates.)
(The enforced envelope is about X -445..-10 and Y -441..-10, so this target sits 5 mm)
(inside the Y end and on the X pull-off edge. Homed, an out-of-envelope target is refused)
(with a soft-limit alarm instead of being driven into the end of travel.)
G53 G0 X-10 Y-436
(print,P116 pen-up, home, and park complete)
o1161 return [1]
